{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I woke up this morning feeling really nauseous and ended up vomiting several times. I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Did you notice any blood in your vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just stomach contents."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good. How’s your blood sugar been?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "This morning it was 285, so I took 13 units of Humalog. It came down to 169, which is better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good job managing that. Have you been taking your metoclopramide and other usual meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been on all my home medications, including metoclopramide. I didn’t eat breakfast because I felt so sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. You’ve had this before with your gastroparesis, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, several times. I have the gastric pacer, and I’ve been following the diet I got last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great you’re staying on the diet. We’ll give you IV fluids to rehydrate and some anti-nausea meds to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. My blood pressure was high earlier—was that a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was elevated—210 over 112 when you were vomiting. But it’s come down to 180 over 88 now, which is better. Likely due to the stress of vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t have a headache or blurry vision, so I wasn’t sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. We’ll keep monitoring it. Your heart rate was also high—116—but that’s common with dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I felt really shaky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started you on Zofran and Ativan for nausea. You also got 2 liters of saline in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did get a dose of Zofran earlier. It helped a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue that and add Compazine if needed. You’re also getting metoclopramide through your port."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my port okay to use? I haven’t needed it in a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we accessed it safely. It’s working well. We’re using it for meds and fluids since you can’t take things by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Should I be worried about my diabetes with not eating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adjusting your insulin. You’re still getting Lantus at night, and we’ll use your sliding scale for corrections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I don’t want my sugars to go too high or low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll check your blood sugar regularly. Your labs this morning showed a glucose of 279, but otherwise your kidney and liver function look normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the lipase test? I remember last time they checked for pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good thinking. Your lipase was normal—only 29—so it’s not pancreatitis. This looks like a typical gastroparesis flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Do you think my pacer needs adjusting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We recommend you follow up with your gastroenterologist in two months to evaluate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already have that appointment. Should I call sooner if things don’t improve?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-05-21 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have persistent vomiting, fevers, chest pain, or trouble breathing, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I haven’t vomited since last night, and the nausea is much less."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your heart rate is down to 88, and your blood pressure is 160 over 90. Much improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel less shaky too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat labs show your hemoglobin dropped a bit—from 13.4 to 11.0—probably from inflammation or mild blood loss, but nothing urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from vomiting? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely related, but we’ll keep an eye on it. You’re not anemic enough to need a transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Can I try some food today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small sips of ginger ale and maybe some toast later. We’ll go slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember the diet—low fat, low fiber, small meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-05-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Nutrition will come by to review it again with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’ve kept down toast and ginger ale all day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel like I’m turning a corner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to switch your meds to oral form. You’ll take metoclopramide by mouth four times a day with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same dose as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 10 mg. We’re also restarting your lisinopril since you’re tolerating fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the clonidine patch?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-05-23 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep that on weekly. Blood pressure is stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. You’re stable and tolerating food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your metoclopramide regularly. Follow the gastroparesis diet closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have Compazine and Ativan for breakthrough nausea—use as needed, but call your doctor if it doesn’t improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual—Lantus at night and Humalog with meals using your sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to check my sugars more often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. And keep that follow-up with your GI doctor to check the pacer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2197-05-24 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything concerns you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-05-21 11:55:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-05-24 13:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer, hypertension, and GERD was admitted for acute nausea and vomiting. She presented with dehydration, elevated blood pressure, and sinus tachycardia, but no signs of pancreatitis or bleeding. She was treated with IV fluids, antiemetics including Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan, and continued on metoclopramide via her port. Her insulin regimen was maintained with Lantus and sliding scale Humalog. Over the hospital stay, her symptoms improved, vital signs normalized, and she advanced to tolerating oral intake with toast and ginger ale. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue her gastroparesis diet, medications, and follow up with gastroenterology to evaluate her gastric pacer.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
